CHAPTER.VERS:
Prepare

          {+}
         the buckler and shield, and draw near to battle.

Harness the horses, and get up, you

          {+}
         horsemen, and stand forth with your

          {+}
         helmets; furbish the spears, put on the coats of mail.

Go up, you

          {+}
         horses; and rage, you

          {+}
         chariots; and let the mighty men go forth: Cush and Put, that handle the shield; and the Ludim, that handle and bend the bow.

Declare

          {+}
         in Egypt, and publish in Migdol, and publish in Memphis and in Tahpanhes: say

          {+}
        , Stand forth, and prepare yourself; for the sword has devoured round about you.

Call

          {+}
         the name of Pharaoh king of Egypt: A noise that let the appointed time pass by.
